 The remaining slow request groups after this pass are intentionally behavior-heavy: signature verification, large ActivityPub pagination fixtures, and media processing. Keep future comparisons uninstrumented and scoped to `spec/requests`; system and streaming suites remain excluded.
+
+## Factory usage optimization (2026-11-23)
+
+The setup-level optimizations above left the most expensive fixture behavior inside the two highest-volume fabricators: `:status` created a bookmark after every save, and `:user` created two login activities after every save. Neither relationship represented behavior shared by the object being fabricated. Specs that actually exercise bookmarks or login activities create those records explicitly.
+
+FactoryProf was run with the same seed immediately before and after removing those callbacks:
+
+```shell
+FPROF=1 bundle exec rspec spec/models --require test_prof --format progress --seed 12533
+FPROF=1 bundle exec rspec spec/requests --require test_prof --format progress --seed 12533
+```
+
+| Group | Run | Examples | Factory calls | Bookmark calls | Login activity calls | Factory top-level time | RSpec time |
+| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Models | Before | 1795 | 3877 | 717 | 270 | 50.500s | 61.57s |
+| Models | After | 1795 | 2894 | 4 | 0 | 39.786s | 51.36s |
+| Requests | Before | 1877 | 4879 | 436 | 1254 | 47.483s | 104.58s |
+| Requests | After | 1877 | 3198 | 9 | 0 | 32.861s | 78.63s |
+
+The callback removal eliminated 2,664 unrelated records. Model RSpec time dropped 16.6%, request RSpec time dropped 24.9%, and the instrumented combined result dropped from 166.15s to 129.99s (21.8%). Top-level factory time measures the elapsed time inside top-level fabrication calls, so nested callbacks are the main cost represented here; it is not equivalent to whole-suite time.
+
+Final uninstrumented runs with the established command shape completed with zero failures:
+
+```shell
+bundle exec rspec spec/models --format progress --profile 30 --seed 12533
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --format progress --profile 30 --seed 12533
+```
+
+| Group | Examples | RSpec time |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Models | 1795 | 37.56s |
+| Requests | 1877 | 64.37s |
+| Combined | 3672 | 101.93s |
+
+The combined result is 4.37 times faster than the original 445.9s RSpec-time baseline. Use the uninstrumented commands for the speed target; FactoryProf itself adds substantial overhead but is useful for controlled factory comparisons.
+
+The remaining factory hotspots are media attachment processing (5.19s in the model profile and 2.04s in the request profile) and the account/user graph. Do not reintroduce after-create records that most examples never request. Create bookmarks and login activities explicitly in the fixtures or contexts that assert their behavior; that keeps factory state representative and makes costly fixture intent visible.
